   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Alto Comisionado de las Naciones Unidas para los Refugiados (ACNUR)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Haut-Commissaire des Nations Unies pour les r&#xe9;fugi&#xe9;s (HCR)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Repr&#xe9;sentation r&#xe9;gional du HCR en Australie</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNHCR Australia regional representation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia hosts almost 60,000 refugees and 80,000 asylum seekers. Most are from the Middle East or Asia. It&#x2019;s estimated that 8,000 people are stateless.  UNHCR&#x2019;s Office in Canberra promotes refugee rights in Australia, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea, Fiji, the Cook Islands, the Federated States of Micronesia, Kiribati, the Marshall Islands, Nauru, Niue, Palau, Samoa, the Solomon Islands, Tonga, Tuvalu and Vanuatu.  UNHCR supports Australia in developing national refugee legislation, increasing refugee status determination capacity, and introducing protection safeguards in immigration procedures. UNHCR also works with Australia on resettlement and building complementary pathways.  For over a decade, Australia has had offshore transfer arrangements with PNG and Nauru for those who seek asylum by boat. UNHCR advocates in relation to the legal and protection concerns of these arrangements and in seeking solutions for those remaining.  This activity shows details of the UNHCR Australia regional representation for 2025 and future years including the budget, funding, expenditure and results. The Australia regional representation coordinates activities in Australia and Papua New Guinea and also covers without a presence New Zealand and the Pacific Islands.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Cette activit&#xe9; montre les d&#xe9;tails de Australie repr&#xe9;sentation r&#xe9;gionale du HCR pour 2025 et les ann&#xe9;es &#xe0; venir, y compris le budget, les financements, les d&#xe9;penses et les r&#xe9;sultats. Le repr&#xe9;sentation r&#xe9;gionale pour l&apos;Australie coordonne les activit&#xe9;s en Australie, Papouasie-Nouvelle-Guin&#xe9;e et couvre &#xe9;galement, sans pr&#xe9;sence, la Nouvelle-Z&#xe9;lande et les &#xee;les du Pacifique.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Le HCR, l&apos;Agence des Nations Unies pour les r&#xe9;fugi&#xe9;s, est une organisation internationale qui a pour mission de sauver des vies, de prot&#xe9;ger les droits des r&#xe9;fugi&#xe9;s et de construire un avenir meilleur pour les r&#xe9;fugi&#xe9;s, les communaut&#xe9;s d&#xe9;plac&#xe9;es et les apatrides.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNHCR, the UN Refugee Agency, is a global organisation dedicated to saving lives, protecting rights and building a better future for refugees, forcibly displaced communities and stateless people.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNHCR&apos;s work is made possible by the generosity of its donors, including dozens of governments, hundreds of companies and their employees, and millions of private individuals who give directly or through UNHCR&apos;s National Partners.</narrative>
  </description>
